@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+---
+type: decision
+status: active
+updated: 2026-11-05
+sources: [.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md, .harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md, commits 5cd1d80 a99a1bf, tests/gate-denied.list, 0005, 0011]
+verified_by: tests/gate.test.sh
+---
+# 0012: Gate shrink: keep the gate, trim what is never used
+
+**Context.** The Top 10 critique item 4b ("replace the 529-line gate with `permissions` rules and a ~50-line gate") was split off in 0005 as a separate design. The analyst's inventory ([gate-shrink-detail](../../../.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md), 552 lines then) found the path helpers (`rel`/`physrel`/`physical`, readable/writable, raw-stream, 109 lines) are the core protection. Usage replay over 881 conductor Bash calls (2026-10-18..10-28) gave 754 allowed: `harness`, `cat`/`ls`, `git log|status|diff --stat|branch`, `gh pr *`, `herdr pane current|get`. Never used: `git show --stat`, `herdr status|pane list|layout|workspace|tab`, `gh issue|run|repo|auth|browse|pr status`, jq as a pipe consumer. Chaining (`;`, `&`) was 44 of 754 calls, pipes 0. No filesystem MCP server is configured.
+
+A last way out was B′: native subagents instead of the harness runner, which would have made the gate unnecessary. The interactive spike (`.harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md`, rejected 2026-11-03) showed subagents die with the conductor ("1 local agent couldn't be moved and was stopped") and report delivery is decoupled from the Stop-hook verify. The harness runner stays, so the gate stays.
+
+**Decision.** Keep the gate and trim it, as the plan's options, now all in place:
+- (g) keyed on hook `agent_type` (v21); (a) one command per call via the quote-aware `scan_command` (0 allowed pipes, 5.8% chained calls become parallel calls; wiki page conductor-shell-one-command); regression list `tests/gate-denied.list` runs in the suite.
+- (e) the deny messages and the Bash policy tables (`BASH_ALLOW`, `GH_ALLOW`, `GIT_DENY*`) sit in one labelled block near the top (a99a1bf).
+- (c) gh is `pr create|view|list|checks|comment|edit|merge` only; (d) `git branch` list-only by regex, no `git show`, herdr `pane get|current` only.
+- (b) no explicit Agent/Workflow/Monitor/NotebookEdit or `mcp__filesystem__*` cases; `claude/agents/conductor.md` `disallowedTools` covers the first four and the hook MATCHER is `Edit|Write|Read|Grep|Glob|Bash`.
+- Also removed in step 5: the `--via` no-op in `harness ask` (5cd1d80); it is now an unknown option (exit 1).
+- Kept: the path helpers and the Bash allowlist. They are what stops `Read bin/harness`, `..`, symlink escapes and raw-stream reads; a gate under 50 lines would have to drop symlink resolution, Glob/Grep scoping and the allowlist.
+- Rejected (f): replacing the gate with `permissions` rules. User-scope rules also bind workers (same settings file), deny beats allow so "deny Read except .harness/docs" cannot be written, and Bash patterns are fragile. Only tool-name denies fit, and (b) already uses them.
+
+**Status.** Active. Supersedes the 4b consequence in [0005](0005-gate-only-inside-herdr.md).
+
+**Consequences.** Gate 552 lines (analyst baseline) → 513 (v21) → 518 with the policy-block banner; most of the trim landed with v21, step 5 only formalised and tested it. A new conductor shell form must be added to `BASH_ALLOW` and `conductor.md` "You may run directly" together. A filesystem MCP server added later would be ungated unless `mcp__filesystem` is added to `disallowedTools`.
